diff --git a/.opencode/skills/money-rules/SKILL.md b/.opencode/skills/money-rules/SKILL.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d164040
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.opencode/skills/money-rules/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+name: money-rules
+description: How ledger-lab parses, stores and formats money amounts. Use it before changing money.ts or an importer.
+---
+
+# Money rules
+
+- Every amount is integer cents (`Cents` in `src/money.ts`). Convert text to cents exactly, by
+  splitting whole and fractional digits; never multiply a float by 100.
+- `parseAmount` accepts an optional leading `-` and `$` and at most two fractional digits.
+- `formatAmount` is the only formatter; reports never build amount strings themselves.
+- A change to amount parsing adds cases for zero, a negative value, one fractional digit and the
+  largest supported value to `src/money.test.ts`.
